subproblems.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and let ν be a finite measure on the Borel sets of ℝ^P. Let V ⊆ ℝ^P be open with ν(ℝ^P ∖ V) = 0. Let β : ℝ^P → Λⁿ(ℝ^P) (Covector (Euclid P) n, normed by the operator norm ‖·‖) be ν-integrable with covectorEuclideanNorm(β(x)) ≤ 1 for ν-a.e. x. Then for every ε > 0 there is an n-form ω : ℝ^P → Λⁿ(ℝ^P) such that:
- ω is C^∞ with compact support (IsTestForm ω);
- tsupport ω ⊆ V;
- covectorEuclideanNorm(ω(x)) ≤ 1 for every x;
- ∫⁻ ofReal(covectorEuclideanNorm(ω(x) − β(x))) dν(x) < ofReal ε.

Let P, n ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P be any set, T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) (GeometricCurrentOn U n), μ a measure on the Borel sets of ℝ^P, ξ : ℝ^P → Λ_n(ℝ^P) (MultiVector P n) and β : ℝ^P → Λⁿ(ℝ^P) (Covector (Euclid P) n, with operator norm ‖·‖). Write |α| := covectorEuclideanNorm α. Assume:
(i) μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U;
(ii) ξ is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(iii) |ξ(x)(α)| ≤ |α| for every x and every n-covector α;
(iv) T(ω) = ∫ ξ(x)(ω(x)) dμ(x) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U);
(v) β is μ-a.e. strongly measurable;
(vi) there is C ∈ ℝ with ‖β(x)‖ ≤ C for every x;
(vii) |β(x)| ≤ 1 for every x;
(viii) ξ(x)(β(x)) = 1 for μ-a.e. x.
Then μ(W′) ≤ M_W(T) = T.massOn W for all sets W, W′ ⊆ ℝ^P such that W′ is open, W′ ⊆ W, and W′ ⊂⊂ U (CompactlyContained W′ U: closure W′ is compact and contained in U).
